A socket is a file descriptor representing a network endpoint. Server side: `socket()` → `bind()` → `listen()` → `accept()` → `read/write`. Client side: `socket()` → `connect()` → `read/write`.

```cpp
// Server (simplified)
int fd = socket(AF_INET, SOCK_STREAM, 0);
bind(fd, (sockaddr*)&addr, sizeof(addr));
listen(fd, 10);
int client = accept(fd, nullptr, nullptr);
read(client, buf, sizeof(buf));
write(client, response, len);
```
